      "privp-updated": "Updated October 14, 2026. Applies to Swipelate on Windows (GitHub and Microsoft Store releases), macOS, the YouTube extension, and this website.",
      "privp-summary": "Summary: Swipelate requires no user account, never sells or shares your data, and displays no ads. Text you highlight to translate is sent only to the translation provider you select. Anonymous stats can be turned off anytime in Settings.",
      "privp-text-title": "Your Translated Text",
      "privp-text-1": "When you highlight text or select a screen area to translate, that text is transmitted to your chosen translation engine in Settings: Google Translate (default), DeepL, Anthropic Claude, or an OpenAI-compatible API endpoint you configure. Each service handles text under its own privacy policy.",
      "privp-text-2": "If \"Automatically use fallback when primary engine fails\" is enabled (default), text may be translated by the offline model on your device, or by another secondary engine you provided an API key for (DeepL, Claude, or OpenAI-compatible API).",
      "privp-text-3": "The Offline engine translates entirely on your device and sends text nowhere.",
      "privp-text-4": "On-screen character recognition (OCR) runs on-device via Windows OCR or Apple Vision. Screen captures are neither stored on disk nor transmitted over the network.",
      "privp-text-5": "When English definition lookup is active, single words are queried via Free Dictionary API, and via Oxford Dictionaries API if you entered their API keys.",
      "privp-text-6": "API keys you enter (DeepL, Anthropic, OpenAI, Oxford) remain solely on your device and are sent only to that respective service.",
      "privp-local-title": "Local Data Storage",
      "privp-local-p": "Settings, translation history, saved vocabulary, pinned clipboard items, and offline translation models are saved inside the application data directory on your machine. They are never sent to any remote server. You can disable or purge translation history in Settings. The Microsoft Store package clears all data upon uninstallation. For the GitHub installer, uninstalling the app does not automatically wipe the data directory: manually delete the <code>com.quicktranslate.app</code> directory in <code>%APPDATA%</code> (Windows) or <code>~/Library/Application Support</code> (macOS) if desired.",
      "privp-stats-title": "Anonymous Statistics",
      "privp-stats-p1": "To track active device counts, the app transmits once daily: a random device token generated at install, version number, and OS name. It never sends your translated text, name, email, or any personally identifiable information. To combat spam, the stats server retains a truncated SHA-256 hash of the request's network subnet per day, never storing the original IP address. You can disable this anytime via \"Send anonymous usage statistics\" in Settings.",
      "privp-stats-p2": "This website counts visits using a similar method (a random token kept in browser storage, at most once per day) and ignores users with Do Not Track enabled. Fonts are served from Google Fonts, meaning your browser connects to Google and transmits its IP address and standard HTTP headers when loading the page.",
      "privp-net-title": "Other Network Connections",
      "privp-net-1": "The GitHub build checks GitHub Releases once daily for updates (can be turned off in About). The Microsoft Store version is updated directly by Microsoft Store.",
      "privp-net-2": "Offline translation models are downloaded from Hugging Face only when you explicitly click Download in Settings.",
      "privp-kids-title": "Children's Privacy",
      "privp-kids-p": "Swipelate does not collect personal information from anyone, including children.",
      "privp-contact-title": "Policy Changes & Contact",
      "privp-contact-p": "Whenever this policy is revised, the update timestamp at the top is changed accordingly. For privacy inquiries, please open an issue at <a href=\"https://github.com/thydynh03/swipelate/issues\" rel=\"noopener\">github.com/thydynh03/swipelate/issues</a>.",
      "privp-tldr-title": "Summary in English",
      "privp-tldr-p": "Swipelate has no accounts, ads or data sales. Text you translate is sent to the translation service you pick (Google Translate by default, DeepL, Anthropic Claude or an OpenAI-compatible API you enter); with fallback on (the default), a failed translation is retried offline, then with another engine you entered a key for. The Offline engine and OCR run on your device. Settings, history, vocabulary and API keys stay on your device. A daily anonymous ping (random install id, version, OS) counts users and can be turned off in Settings; for abuse protection the stats server keeps a truncated SHA-256 hash of the sender's network per day, never the IP address. The website loads fonts from Google Fonts. The GitHub build checks GitHub for updates; the Microsoft Store build is updated by the Store. Contact: GitHub issues.",
